{
  "slug": "logfire",
  "name": "Logfire",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Add Logfire observability to Python applications with auto-instrumentation for FastAPI, httpx, asyncpg, SQLAlchemy, and more",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **4 commands** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `logfire-evals` (Evaluate Python AI/agent code against a dataset of test cases using pydantic_evals, and review results in Logfire's Datasets…), `logfire-infrastructure` (Monitor hosts, Docker containers, Kubernetes clusters, database/queue/cache servers, and cloud-provider metrics with Pydantic Logfire — no application code…), `logfire-instrumentation` (Add Pydantic Logfire observability to application code — traces, logs, metrics, and AI/agent spans), `logfire-query` (Query and analyze Logfire telemetry data — traces, logs, spans, metrics, summaries, and SQL results), `logfire-setup` (Entry point for Pydantic Logfire — an observability, monitoring, and evals platform), `logfire-ui` (Open or return Logfire project pages, live views, trace links, and Explore pages in the Codex browser without…)\n- **Commands** (4): `debug` (Use Logfire traces to investigate errors and debug production issues), `dev-session` (Start a local Logfire dev session to send traces from your running app for debugging), `instrument` (Detect languages and frameworks in the current project and add Logfire instrumentation), `query` (Query Logfire telemetry data interactively or add query capabilities to code)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `logfire`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install logfire@claude-plugins-official` from `pydantic/skills` (`plugins/logfire`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
